            <ArticleTitle>Concomitant cerebral and coronary subclavian steal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>853-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the unusual presentation of simultaneous coronary and cerebrovascular insufficiency secondary to subclavian steal in a patient previously treated with coronary artery bypass grafting. Movement of the arm produced reversal of flow (&quot;steal&quot;) in both the left vertebral and left internal thoracic arteries and resulted in the onset of angina and neurologic symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
